artifact_set.bazel_swift_handoff:
Wave-3 dive bazel/rules-swift writes to swift-bazel/. At authoring time:
- draft rules/bazel-quality/swift.md (BZL-SWIFT) inside the published bazel-quality set, with a never-matching glob, never a bundle member;
- add a routing row and keywords (rules_swift, swift_library, swift_binary, swift.toolchain) to the bazel-quality index, and name swift-quality in its Siblings;
- bump publish.toml [rules.bazel-quality] 0.3.0 -> 0.4.0 and update docs/bazel-quality.md.
The file is framed 'if you adopt Bazel for Swift' (5/40). Bazel is installed from the ocx index into ~/.cache/research-lang/bazel-tools; otherwise rows are marked unverified: read only.
